examples.question_text:
The graph shows the cost $C$ and revenue $R$, in dollars, for making and selling $n$ snack packs.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.8cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\path[use as bounding box] (-1.9,-0.9) rectangle (6.5,6.5);
\definecolor{revenueBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{costRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=1,gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.4,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.4);
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x/\n in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50,6/60}{\draw[black] (\x,0.07)--(\x,-0.07);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.07) {$\n$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/60,2/120,3/180,4/240,5/300,6/360}{\draw[black] (0.07,\y)--(-0.07,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.07,\y) {$\v$};}
\node[below] at (3,-0.6) {Snack packs ($n$)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.6,3) {Money (\$)};
\draw[revenueBlue,thick] (0,0)--(6,6);
\draw[costRed,thick] (0,1.5)--(6,4.5);
\node[above left] at (5.7,5.7) {$R$};
\node[below right] at (5.3,4.15) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Use the graph to find the break-even quantity and revenue.
(b) Use the graph to find the profit or loss when $50$ snack packs are sold.

examples.solution_text:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.8cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\path[use as bounding box] (-1.9,-0.9) rectangle (6.5,6.5);
\definecolor{revenueBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{costRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=1,gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (6,6);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.4,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6.4);
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x/\n in {1/10,2/20,3/30,4/40,5/50,6/60}{\draw[black] (\x,0.07)--(\x,-0.07);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.07) {$\n$};}
\foreach \y/\v in {1/60,2/120,3/180,4/240,5/300,6/360}{\draw[black] (0.07,\y)--(-0.07,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.07,\y) {$\v$};}
\node[below] at (3,-0.6) {Snack packs ($n$)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.6,3) {Money (\$)};
\draw[revenueBlue,thick] (0,0)--(6,6);
\draw[costRed,thick] (0,1.5)--(6,4.5);
\node[above left] at (5.7,5.7) {$R$};
\node[below right] at (5.3,4.15) {$C$};
\draw[black,dashed] (3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3);
\fill[black] (3,3) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above left] at (3,3) {$(30,180)$};
\draw[black,dashed] (5,0)--(5,5)--(0,5);
\draw[black,dashed] (5,4)--(0,4);
\fill[black] (5,5) circle (1.5pt);
\fill[black] (5,4) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) The revenue and cost lines intersect at $(30,180)$. Break-even is $30$ snack packs, with revenue of $\$180$.

(b) At $n=50$, the graph gives $R=300$ and $C=240$.
$\begin{align*}P&=R-C\\&=300-240\\&=60\end{align*}$
The profit is $\$60$.
